/node_modules/

# The build. `dist/` is what Pages serves and `.types/` is the declarations `composite` insists on emitting, which
# nothing serves and nothing reads except the project next door.
/dist/
/.types/

# The two indexes `scripts/validate-gpx.mts --write` derives from the GPX files, which `pnpm build` runs before it
# assembles `dist/`. Tracked they were a second copy of what `git ls-files` and the `<pgr:event>` fields already say,
# kept in step by a check that could only ever report the copy was stale.
/data/entries-by-event.json
/data/gpx-paths.json

# `tsc -b` needs `composite` in both projects, and `composite` writes a build cache per project. The browser one is
# named into `.types/` above, since its default position is derived from `outDir` and so falls inside the artifact;
# `scripts/` emits nothing, so its own stays beside its config.
/scripts/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Every subtask gets its own worktree and the harness puts them here, so this holds another branch's checkout rather
# than anything of this one's. `.prettierignore` and `eslint.config.mjs` exclude it for the same reason.
/.claude/worktrees/
